Name recognition provided no help to Alan Grayson's family this year.
Star Grayson, daughter of liberal U.S. Rep. Alan Grayson, was the last of three Graysons to lose an election this year.
A senior at Olympia High School, Star Grayson, who turned 18 this month, was bidding to make history as Florida's youngest elected official.
But she finished a distant third Tuesday in the three-person race for a seat on the Orange County Soil & Water Conservation District Board of Supervisors. Lawyer Michael Barber won with 42 percent of the vote, community activist Maria Bolton-Joubert took 38 percent, and Star Grayson got 20 percent.
