The Bolshoi Ballet is calling its current visit to North America its ��Great Tour.�� The company landed in Toronto this week for the first time in 33 years and it��s marking its return with the ever-popular Swan Lake. And, while not flawless, there were indeed moments of greatness in the opening performance Tuesday evening.
The Tchaikovsky-scored ballet got its roots at the Bolshoi. It was first choreographed in 1877 for the troupe by Marius Petipa and Lev Ivanov. Countless choreographers have since put their own personal touch on the ballet and this particular version was revised in 2001 by the Bolshoi��s former director Yuri Grigorovich.
