Queensland Health Minister Lawrence Springborg says the addition of new intensive care beds and a helipad to the Rockhampton Hospital are a boon for the community.
The Central Queensland Hospital and Health Service will spend $12 million on 10 intensive care unit (ICU) beds and $5 million on the helipad on top of the ward block redevelopment.
